+- Replace hardcoded ACCESS_TOKEN, PHONE_NUMBER_ID, VERIFY_TOKEN, BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID with `os.getenv()`
+- These are currently committed to GitHub in plain text
+
+### 1.2 Clean secrets from documentation
+- Remove Supermemory API key from `INTEGRATION_STATUS.md`
+
+### 1.3 Credential rotation (manual — Adedayo)
+- Rotate Meta WhatsApp ACCESS_TOKEN in Facebook Developer Console
+- Rotate Supermemory API key
+- Set new values as environment variables in Railway
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2: WEBHOOK CONSOLIDATION (Day 2-3)
+
+### Current State (3 entry points):
+- `main.py` `/webhook` → V5 handler (Twilio)
+- `routers/webhook.py` `/api/webhook` → V5 handler (Meta)
+- `routers/webhook.py` `/api/webhook/twilio` → UnifiedTadeHandler (Twilio)
+- `channels/twilio_whatsapp.py` `/webhook/twilio` → Another Twilio handler
+
+### Target State (2 entry points, one router):
+- `routers/webhook.py` `/api/webhook` → V5 handler (Meta) ✅ keep as-is
+- `routers/webhook.py` `/api/webhook/twilio` → V5 handler (Twilio) ← fix this
+
+### Changes:
+1. **`routers/webhook.py`**: Change `/api/webhook/twilio` to call `message_handler_v5.handle_message()` instead of `UnifiedTadeHandler`
+2. **`main.py`**: DELETE the inline `/webhook` endpoint (lines 536-594) and `_process_and_respond` function
+3. **`main.py`**: REMOVE `from app.channels import twilio_whatsapp` and its router include
+4. **`channels/twilio_whatsapp.py`**: DELETE file (duplicate)
+
+### Verification:
+- Both Meta and Twilio messages should flow through V5 agent chain
+- `grep -r "UnifiedTadeHandler" app/ --include="*.py"` returns nothing in active code
+
+---
+
